def bc(l,pgs,t,a,f):
 locators=[]
 for pg in pgs:
  lines=pages[pg-389].splitlines();start=next(i for i,s in enumerate(lines,1)if s.strip());end=max(i for i,s in enumerate(lines,1)if s.strip());locators.append(dict(source='WB51',pdf_page=pg,printed_page=pg-9,physical_text_first_line=start,physical_text_last_line=end,source_first_line_sha256=ht(lines[start-1].strip()),source_span_sha256=ht('\n'.join(lines[start-1:end])),page_extracted_text_sha256=ht(pages[pg-389]),context_span_kind='whole physical text page including surrounding diagram/prose'))
 branches.append(dict(lesson=l,pdf_pages=pgs,printed_pages=[p-9 for p in pgs],topic=t,branch_paraphrase=a,family_dependencies=f.split(),primary_source_page_locators=locators,source_study='documentary only',original_execution='not run',candidate_execution='not run',verified=False))
bc('WB31',[389,390],'Anchor choices, display hardware and character geometry','Source distinguishes paragraph,page and character anchoring. Guided character box stays in the title line with bottom alignment and WrapNo. Width.4in/AutoHeight changes star height to.296in; parenthesized dimension labels indicate automatic adjustment. Graphics-card absence prevents viewing but source offers optional printer output if graphics-capable. No hardware or installed image is accessed.','G1 L1 P1 P3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[390,391,392],'Figure-to-UserBox conversion, image replacement and copied owner','Box type changes inside the existing definition from Figure to UserBox,whose style has no border. Filename BUTTRFLY.WPG replaces STAR-5.WPG after Yes. Block/Left2 selects the whole character-box owner;Move/Block/Copy and Enter create a second box. FlushRight aligns its left edge with the margin,requiring AdvanceLeft.4in to bring its right edge into the margin. ReplacementNo/Cancel and missing images remain pending.','G1 L3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB31',[392,393,394],'Drop-cap deletion, font metrics and figure options before owner','Delete initial R then recreate it as Bold text in a Figure,left aligned with Roman25pt and AutoBoth sizing. FigureOptions must precede Figure1. Set None on four borders and outside spaces Left0,Right.1,Top0,Bottom0. UserBox could remove a border alone,but options are needed for spacing too. Later figures may inherit active options;not an isolated per-box settings claim.','G1 L1 E1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[394],'Menu text without mouse icons and notice206','Original printed385 has textual menu alternatives after steps3and7 but no icons. Notice206 adds the two icons. The routes are already counted as original menu alternatives;icons do not add numbered steps or prove physical clicking. This batch has only one explicit physical mouse paragraph,elsewhere in WB33.','G1 I3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[395,396],'Page-anchored callout placement and inherited TextBox options','Page anchor places callout across columns2–3 at vertical6in,width4.17in and auto height. Place its owner at page top after ColumnDefinition;otherwise source warns of next-page placement or wrong column behavior. Roman15ptItalic/Bold text is entered. Default TextBox thick borders/shading are suppressed by earlier headline TextBoxOptions;this inherited context explains missing top line/shading.','G1 L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[396,397],'Reset callout border/shading and outside spacing','A new TextBoxOptions before TextBox2 restores top/bottomThick,left/rightNone,10percent shading and.1in outside top/bottom spacing with zero sides. Earlier headline options remain;scope follows owner ordering. Preview is source expectation only. Unknown options,native option-owner bytes and cancellation invariants remain open.','G1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[397,398],'Vertical-line current cursor position and unequal column lengths','Create first vertical line right of column1 from its top. SetPosition displays current caret height and computes length to column bottom. For separator right of column2,move to top of longer column3 before creating;set BetweenColumns2. This avoids measuring against shorter column2. Status Col1/3 and caret context are required preconditions.','G1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[398,399,400],'Split separator around callout with measured coordinates','Preview shows separator crossing callout. Record example top2.32in,above5.62in,below7.37in. Edit upper segment length5.62−2.32=3.3in;create lower segment at7.37in and let source compute remaining length. These are illustrative measurements tied to selected layout/resources,not universal original coordinates. Optional EditVertical can adjust either line further.','G1 L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[400,401,402],'Overlay order, two wrap settings and unnamed block save/retrieve','First butterfly Figure2 needs WrapNo so copied Figure3 can occupy same region;if first is Yes,the second moves below. SaveF10/Enter then Retrieve/Enter copies a selected graphics box without a stated filename;do not invent a disk target or claim source-file conservation from an unrun route. List*.wpg selects BKGRND-1.WPG,Yes replaces copied butterfly,and second WrapYes pushes body text below both.','G1 E3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB31',[401],'Graphics provenance is edition-specific and conversion remains open','Source says supplied WPGs were created with DrawPerfect and predicts first-quarter1990 availability. Retain this1989-era provenance statement,not current product advice. Selecting/retrieving WPG is not GRAPHCNV execution or G2completion. All image availability and byte compatibility require later qualified original evidence.','G1 G2 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[402,403],'Graphics edit scale/pan/rotate/mirror and reset variants','Image editor PageDown9reduces scale;ScaleX7/ScaleY7fine tune. UnequalX/Y can stretch horizontally/vertically. Original Up8,Rotate45degrees left,Enter retains nonmirrored image,thenLeft8. GoToCtrlHome restores original size/proportions;mirrorYes and free experiments are optional leads. Before continuing,return page2 in View. No resource image is edited here.','G1 P3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[403],'Later374 changes movement repetitions only','Notice374 changes Up and Left repetitions in steps7/10 from eight to four. Original eight-count instructions and later four-count correction remain separate;PageDown9andScale7/7are unchanged by this notice. No selected executable or image-editor increment size is inferred.','G1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[403,404,405],'Native TABLE.WKB inside graphics box and drop shadow alternatives','Retrieve TABLE.WKB into Figure4,HorizontalFull. This is native document content inside a box,not a WPG conversion or ordinary body Retrieve. InsideLeft.15in offsets table;other inside edges remain zero as instructed. All four borders exist;Thick or ExtraThick on two adjacent sides makes a drop shadow. Guided right/bottomExtraThick,left/topSingle. Full positioning is kept as the source choice without assuming full physical-page width.','G1 E3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB31',[405],'Saved NEWSLTR and optional printer/font adaptation','Save learner NEWSLTR separate from original NEWSLTR.WKB. Printing is optional and requires selecting own printer,with likely font/layout adjustments from WorkbookPrinter. No physical print job,resource read or save occurs;missing printer/font,overwrite/refusal and native-image conservation remain pending.','G1 L1 P1 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB32',[406,407],'Sort input/output Screen versus named file','Screen input sorts retrieved records;Screen output replaces in-memory records. Named output leaves screen records undisturbed and writes a separate file. Original CUSTOMER.WKB is used,not WB24learner CUSTOMER with filled Ted address. Sort menu appears under records;no actual file is sorted. Initial line-sort default changes to Merge.','A5 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB32',[407,408,409,410],'Key schema, alphanumeric/numeric and negative line/word indices','Up to nine keys contain type,field,line,word. Guided typea stays alphanumeric;numeric is a source lead for unequal-length numbers/dates,not proof of date parsing. Field2contains addresses with varying line/word counts. Negative1counts from bottom/right,so a 2 -1 -1 targets ZIP. View/Exit inspects Jayna while preserving key editor context.','A5 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB32',[410,411,412],'Missing address ordering, retained settings and descending file','Ascending source result places Ted first because address field is empty;Kathleen is lowest nonempty ZIP,Samuel highest. Next Sort retains type/key;CUSTOMER.ZIPoutput writes descending result while screen retains prior data. Switch to document2 and Retrieve inspects Samuel first. Missing-field/tie/descending-empty behavior beyond depicted examples remains pending.','A5 I1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB32',[412],'Merge preserves sorted secondary record order','ExitNoYes closes document2;ExitNoNo clears document1. Merge original STORES.WKB with learner CUSTOMER.ZIP;source expects first letter SamuelA.Roberts,matching first sorted record. Discard result. No original secondary is rewritten or opened by the research;save/failure/cancel behavior remains unobserved.','A5 I1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB32',[412,413],'Two name keys and existing HardSpace token boundary','Last-name key a 1 1 -1 handles optional middle names;second key a 1 1 1 orders equal last names by first name. Right navigation populates second default key. Existing HardSpace between Corrales, and Jr. makes the pair one sort word;Reveal shows bracketed space. It is inspected,not inserted in this exercise. No general locale/collation/tie-stability claim.','A5 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB32',[414,415],'Select-before-sort key roles and explicit OR syntax','Key1a 2 -1 -1 sorts by ZIP;key2a 2 -1 1 tests Boston;key3a 2 -1 2 tests York. Literal key2=boston + key3=york requires spaces around plus,which means OR. Source expects actionSelectAndSort,Ascending,MergeSort and Kathleen before Joseph. Other select symbols are unselected reference leads;NoMatch,syntax errors,Cancel and malformed keys need later evidence.','A5 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB32',[410,413,414,415],'Expected Joseph result conflicts with illustrated Manhattan address','The original public pictures identify Joseph address last line Manhattan, NY10036. That would not supply York as the second word tested by key3. Yet the final prose expects Joseph selected by the Boston/York predicate. Predicate also does not require first wordNew. Preserve exact keys,expected named result and conflicting diagrams;do not silently change city/data/predicate or claim a successful original sort. No Lesson32notice appears in the registered notice text.','A5 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[416,425],'Conditional initial style library cleanup and later1643','Original list is initially empty unless SetupStyleLibraryFilename retrieves definitions. Conditional Delete5/DefinitionOnly3clears these before creation;later1643also names installed LIBRARY.STY and repeats until all removed. Source does not bound library size or provide refusal/Cancel sequence. Setup auto-retrieval is an optional persistent-resource lead,no actual library read or deletion.','D1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[417,418,419],'Open/paired/outline style types and comment divider','Paired default has On/Off owners around selected or newly typed text;Open single owner affects later document. Outline is an earlier lesson18lead. Paired StyleEditor Comment is a divider representing document text:owners before it go intoOn,after it intoOff. EnterHRt option appears for paired styles and disappears forOpen;its full behavior is not exercised.','D1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB33',[418,419],'Headings selection alternatives, auto off and name inconsistency','First heading BlockAltF4/End,mouse drag,or EditBlock/End then apply Headings. On containsUND;Off automatically receivesund. Repeat for two named headings without adding original numbers. Source prose singularHeading conflicts with created Headings and pictured Headings;retain original labels. General font restoration example and paired-code boundaries remain native/runtime questions.','D1 I3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB33',[419,420,421],'Masthead paired-first typing and restoration state','Masthead Roman18pt,Bold,Center is applied before typing HALVAHerald. Before OpenFormat exists,source Off includes Helvetica10pt andbold-off. Source says Off restores current document formats,giving Roman10/Helvetica12example elsewhere. Per-instance versus definition-wide restoration and updates after later OpenFormat application cannot be concluded from pictures;qualified native fixtures remain required.','D1 L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB33',[421,422,423],'Draft OpenFormat includes nested header/date and document defaults','Format open style contains HeaderAEveryPage with NEWSLETTER DRAFT--Terry Brown,FlushRight Printed on plus DateCode,BottomRightpage number,double line spacing andCourier10cpi. Open applies before masthead/body;preview100or200checks font. Date is a live DateCode source instruction,not a fixed modern date or user author value. Nested header/native owner scope is unverified.','D1 L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB33',[424,425],'STY library versus embedded document definitions and retrieval without application','Save whole list DRAFT.STY;extension optional. NEWSLTR.DFTembeds draft definitions and document formatting. Retrieving NEWSTEXT.WKB then DRAFT.STYloads available definitions but does not automatically insert their style owners;application is optional before discarding. External library,embedded snapshot and later edits have separate save histories. Unknown/corrupt/missing library and overwrite paths are pending.','D1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[425,426],'Editing one definition updates all uses and correction2064 drift','Headings edit removesUND,addsHelvetica12ptItalic+Bold and new description. All three current-document uses change after one definition edit. Original step11PrintView100then12PageDown differs from2064reversed11/12;notice declares407but matching section is actual416–417,and steps11/12on417. Do not reorder original count or infer target resources. DRAFT.STYis not rewritten by this edit unless explicitly saved.','D1 L1 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[426,427],'Cancel/Restore copies deleted horizontal lines and Advance owners','Masthead code editing creates HLinewidth.04/shading50. Backspace deletes it,CancelF1/Restore1returns it,then a second Restore inserts same line after comment. Similarly delete/restore AdvanceDown.15andRestorecopy before lowerHLine. These are explicit deletion-restore/copy operations within StyleEditor,not generic abort cancellation. Last-deletion/history interactions and owner bytes need later evidence.','D1 G3 L3 E1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB33',[427,428,429],'GraphicOnDisk style reference versus embedded image','Actual figure cannot be stored in style;source automatically sets GraphicOnDisk when BUTTRFLY.WPG is assigned in style. Only filename is stored,then resolved for View/print,unlike ordinary embedded-figure document retrieval. CharacterCenter,.4inAutoHeight,WrapNo;Backspace/Restorecopies box on both sides of comment;FlushRight then AdvanceLeft.4corrects right edge. Missing/relative external reference resolution remains unspecified and unexecuted.','D1 G1 L3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[429],'Three style-deletion alternatives and IncludingCodes selection','First two deletion choices remove document Style owners,either retaining direct format owners or deleting them with styles. Third deletes definition only and leaves Style owners. Guided IncludingCodes2removes singleOpenFormatanditsformats plus list definition,then recreates Format. Source gives no exact refusal/Cancel sequence or orphan-definition rendering contract;do not infer one.','D1 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[430,431],'Final OpenFormat excludes ColumnsOn and optional paired-column design','New FormatOpen containsRoman10pt,FullJustification and default two-newspaper-column definition. Exit Columns menu instead of On because style is at document start above masthead. Source offers alternative separate paired style with ColumnDefinition+On for onlyarticles,without complete numbered route. Step2says name of description despite choosingName;retain wording mismatch.','D1 L1 L6 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB33',[431,432],'Reinsert Format and place ColumnsOn at first article','IncludingCodes removed oldOpenFormat,so new definition must be applied anew at page start. Then Down4/Leftlocates HeadingsStyleOn before first article;ColumnsOnoutsideFormatstyle starts columns below masthead. Preview describes final lines,butterflies,italicbold headings and two columns;save FINAL.STYlist. No underlying native layout is executed.','D1 L6 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[432,433],'Same-name library collision, replaceYes and add-other semantics','Retrieve DRAFT.STY into final list raises Style(s)already exist.Replace?Yes replaces Format,Headings,Masthead definitions/descriptions/codes;other incoming names are added. Preview source claims draftformat restoration. No/Cancel,duplicate names,partial library errors,atomic save or unchanged-original native artifacts remain pending. Optional FINAL.STYreload,editing or own styles is open-ended.','D1 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB33',[430,431,432,433],'External ColumnsOn owner versus all-final-formats-replaced claim','Final ColumnsOn was explicitly inserted outside the Format style. After replacing definitions,the source says all final formatting becomes draft and shows one-column draft. It does not explain external ColumnsOn persistence or how removing ColumnDefinition changes its interpretation. Preserve both instructions and claimed picture;do not invent library retrieval deleting unrelated document owners.','D1 L6 Q1 Q2 Q3')
